sequenceDiagram
  actor Operator as CUSTODIAN or ADMIN
  actor Technician as Assigned MAINTAINER
  participant Page as Maintenance React pages
  participant API as MaintenanceController
  participant Service as MaintenanceService Spring proxy
  participant Directory as JdbcTechnicianDirectoryAdapter
  participant Equipment as JdbcEquipmentMaintenanceAdapter
  participant Case as MaintenanceCase
  participant State as MaintenanceStateMachine
  participant Repo as JdbcMaintenanceCaseRepository
  participant History as JdbcMaintenanceHistoryRepository
  participant Events as SpringMaintenanceEventPublisher
  participant Spring as ApplicationEventPublisher
  participant DB as PostgreSQL
  Note over API,Service: Principal supplies actor ID, service policy checks role and self.<br/>Writes need Session and CSRF, no client expectedVersion or If-Match.
  Operator->>Page: Assign OPEN case to selected technician
  Page->>API: POST cases/id/assignment with technicianId
  API->>Service: assignTechnician(caseId, technicianId, actorId)
  Note over Service,DB: Spring begins assignment transaction
  Service->>Repo: findById(caseId)
  Repo->>DB: SELECT case snapshot without row lock
  DB-->>Repo: OPEN case and persisted version
  Repo-->>Service: Restored MaintenanceCase
  Service->>Directory: ensureTechnician(technicianId)
  Directory->>DB: Check ACTIVE account and MAINTAINER role
  Service->>Equipment: lockForMaintenance(equipmentId)
  Equipment->>DB: SELECT Equipment status FOR UPDATE
  Service->>Case: assign(technicianId)
  Case->>State: transition(OPEN, ASSIGN)
  State-->>Case: ASSIGNED
  Service->>Repo: update(item using initial snapshot version)
  Repo->>DB: UPDATE case WHERE id and version RETURNING fields
  Note over Repo,DB: V002 check_maintenance guards transition,<br/>maintenance_version increments version, V004 makes it bigint.
  alt Row updated and all synchronous processing succeeds
    DB-->>Repo: Saved ASSIGNED snapshot and new version
    Repo-->>Service: Restored saved case
    Service->>History: append(ASSIGN history)
    History->>DB: INSERT SUCCESS MAINTENANCE_ASSIGN audit
    Service->>Events: publish(MaintenanceAssigned)
    Events->>Spring: publishEvent(event)
    Note over Spring: Main has no production UC04 notification subscriber.
    Service->>DB: Spring transaction commits
    Service-->>API: Case copy
    API-->>Page: 200 ASSIGNED case
  else No row updated or write/consumer failure
    Note over Service: Version conflict or propagated write/consumer failure
    Service->>DB: Spring transaction rolls back
    API-->>Page: Safe ProblemDetail, refresh case
  end
  Technician->>Page: Start own assigned case
  Page->>API: POST cases/id/start
  API->>Service: startMaintenance(caseId, actorId)
  Note over Service,DB: Separate start transaction
  Service->>Repo: findById(caseId) for equipment reference
  Repo->>DB: SELECT snapshot
  Service->>Equipment: lockForMaintenance(equipmentId)
  Equipment->>DB: SELECT Equipment FOR UPDATE
  Service->>Repo: findById(caseId) after lock
  Repo->>DB: Reload current case and version
  Repo-->>Service: Current ASSIGNED case
  Note over Service,Case: requireAssignedTechnician(item, actorId)
  Service->>Case: start()
  Case->>State: transition(ASSIGNED, START)
  State-->>Case: IN_PROGRESS
  Service->>Repo: update(item)
  Repo->>DB: Conditional UPDATE RETURNING trigger version
  Service->>History: append(START history)
  History->>DB: INSERT SUCCESS MAINTENANCE_START audit
  Service->>DB: Spring transaction commits
  API-->>Page: 200 IN_PROGRESS case
  Note over Service,Events: No UC04 start event is published.
  opt Diagnosis, repair action or note before completion
    Page->>API: POST cases/id/diagnosis, repair-actions or notes with detail
    API->>Service: recordDiagnosis, recordRepairAction or addMaintenanceNote
    Service->>Repo: findById(caseId) for equipment reference
    Repo->>DB: SELECT snapshot
    Service->>Equipment: Lock Equipment in a separate work transaction
    Equipment->>DB: SELECT Equipment FOR UPDATE
    Service->>Repo: Reload case, require assigned actor and IN_PROGRESS
    Repo->>DB: SELECT current snapshot
    Service->>History: append(work detail)
    History->>DB: INSERT maintenance audit, no case UPDATE
    Service->>DB: Spring transaction commits
    API-->>Page: 200 unchanged case state and version
  end
  Technician->>Page: Resolve with completion note
  Page->>API: POST cases/id/resolve with resolutionNote
  API->>Service: resolve(caseId, note, actorId)
  Note over Service,DB: Separate completion transaction, failures roll back all writes.
  Service->>Repo: findById(caseId) for equipment reference
  Repo->>DB: SELECT snapshot
  Service->>Equipment: lockForMaintenance(equipmentId)
  Equipment->>DB: SELECT Equipment FOR UPDATE
  Service->>Repo: findById(caseId) after lock
  Repo->>DB: Reload current case and version
  Repo-->>Service: IN_PROGRESS case
  Note over Service,Case: Require assigned actor, non-blank note and valid completion time.
  Service->>Case: resolve(note, clock.instant())
  Case->>State: transition(IN_PROGRESS, RESOLVE)
  State-->>Case: RESOLVED
  Service->>Repo: update(terminal item)
  Repo->>DB: Conditional UPDATE note, status and resolved_at RETURNING version
  DB-->>Repo: Saved RESOLVED snapshot
  Repo-->>Service: Restored saved case
  Service->>Equipment: recomputeAfterResolvedMaintenance(equipmentId)
  Equipment->>DB: Read locked Equipment, query other active cases and ACTIVE loans
  Note over Equipment,DB: RETIRED > other active case > ACTIVE loan > AVAILABLE.<br/>Avoid same-state Equipment UPDATE.
  Equipment->>DB: UPDATE Equipment status when different
  Service->>History: append(RESOLVE history)
  History->>DB: INSERT SUCCESS MAINTENANCE_RESOLVE audit
  Service->>Events: publish(MaintenanceCompleted)
  Events->>Spring: publishEvent(event)
  opt Draft PR 12 consumer only, absent from main
    Note over Spring,DB: MaintenanceNotificationListener requests a deduplicated notice<br/>for the original reporter in the same transaction.<br/>Assignment requests target the assigned technician.
  end
  alt All writes and synchronous consumers succeed
    Service->>DB: Spring transaction commits
    API-->>Page: 200 terminal case
    Page->>Page: Refresh case, history, queues and reports
  else Any failure
    Service->>DB: Spring transaction rolls back case, Equipment and audit
    API-->>Page: Safe ProblemDetail
  end
  Note over Case,Equipment: Unrepairable uses markUnrepairable and MARK_UNREPAIRABLE.<br/>After terminal persistence, markRetired replaces recomputation.<br/>Invalid roles, assignment or transitions abort before success writes/events.
